{
  "slug": "mcp-yoshi",
  "name": "Mcp Yoshi",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Real-time security filter for MCP tool communications. Works as a Claude Code hook to inspect all data sent to and\nreceived from MCP servers. Detects prompt injection, API key leakage, tool poisoning, ASCII smuggling, SSRF,\nBase64-encoded payloads, and Rug Pull attacks. Provides PASS/WARN/BLOCK decisions with per-server configuration,\nallowlisting, and logging. Zero dependencies, ~60ms latency.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 command** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (1): `mcp-yoshi` (Check MCP communication security filter status and configuration)\n- **Hooks** (2): `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mcp-yoshi@claude-community` from `aliksir/mcp-yoshi`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 2,
    "command": 1
  },
